   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi,<div><br></div><div>I&#39;d like to plot an unrooted tree that illustrates the presence/absence of each tip in multiple environments.  Is it possible to do this with gheatmap, or must the tree be rectangular?  I&#39;ve tried modifying the following, I run into some issues in that the unrooted plots, but the heatmap is still vertically oriented.</div><div>(identical to website, w exception that layout=&quot;unrooted&quot; is added to ggtree: <a href=\"https://www.bioconductor.org/packages/release/bioc/vignettes/ggtree/inst/doc/advanceTreeAnnotation.html#visualize-tree-with-associated-matrix\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.bioconductor.org/packages/release/bioc/vignettes/ggtree/inst/doc/advanceTreeAnnotation.html%23visualize-tree-with-associated-matrix&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792482897838000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3zvZAUFiFgybByzeGjWJlr\">https://www.bioconductor.org/packages/release/bioc/vignettes/ggtree/inst/doc/advanceTreeAnnotation.html#visualize-tree-with-associated-matrix</a>)</div><div><br></div><div><pre style=\"box-sizing:border-box;overflow:auto;padding:9.5px;margin-bottom:10px;line-height:1.42857143;color:rgb(51,51,51);word-break:break-all;word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(245,245,245);border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);border-top-left-radius:4px;border-top-right-radius:4px;border-bottom-right-radius:4px;border-bottom-left-radius:4px\"><code style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-size:inherit;color:inherit;background-color:transparent;border-top-left-radius:0px;border-top-right-radius:0px;border-bottom-right-radius:0px;border-bottom-left-radius:0px;white-space:pre-wrap\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">beast_file</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">&lt;-</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">system.file</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">(</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;examples/MCC_FluA_H3.tree&quot;</span>, <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">package</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">=</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;ggtree&quot;</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">)</span>\r\n<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">beast_tree</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">&lt;-</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">read.beast</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">(</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">beast_file</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">)</span>\r\n\r\n<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">genotype_file</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">&lt;-</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">system.file</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">(</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;examples/Genotype.txt&quot;</span>, <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">package</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">=</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;ggtree&quot;</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">)</span>\r\n<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">genotype</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">&lt;-</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">read.table</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">(</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">genotype_file</span>, <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">sep</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">=</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;\\t&quot;</span>, <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">stringsAsFactor</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">=</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(153,0,115)\">F</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">)</span>\r\n<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">p</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">&lt;-</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">ggtree</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">(</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">beast_tree</span>, <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">mrsd</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">=</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;2013-01-01&quot;, layout=&quot;unrooted&quot;</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">)</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">+</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">geom_treescale</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">(</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">x</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">=</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,153,153)\">2008</span>, <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">y</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">=</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,153,153)\">1</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">)</span>\r\n<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">p</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">&lt;-</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">p</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">+</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">geom_tiplab</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">(</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">size</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">=</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,153,153)\">3</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">)</span>\r\n<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">gheatmap</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">(</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">p</span>, <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">genotype</span>, <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">offset</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">=</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,153,153)\">2</span>, <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">width</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">=</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,153,153)\">0.5</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">)</span></code></pre></div><div><br></div><div><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\">The documentation associated with the function &quot;<span style=\"font-size:10pt\">append a heatmap of a matrix to right side of phylogenetic tree&quot; </span>gives me the impression what I&#39;m hoping to do is not possible at present with this function, is that right?  Would you have any alternatives to suggest?  I&#39;ve played with msaplot some as well, but also ran into similar problems.</font></div><div><br></div><div><pre style=\"margin-bottom:10px;padding:9.5px;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);box-sizing:border-box;overflow:auto;line-height:1.42857143;color:rgb(51,51,51);word-break:break-all;word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(245,245,245);border-top-left-radius:4px;border-top-right-radius:4px;border-bottom-right-radius:4px;border-bottom-left-radius:4px\"><code style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-size:inherit;color:inherit;background-color:transparent;border-top-left-radius:0px;border-top-right-radius:0px;border-bottom-right-radius:0px;border-bottom-left-radius:0px;white-space:pre-wrap\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">fasta</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">&lt;-</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">system.file</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">(</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;examples/FluA_H3_AA.fas&quot;</span>, <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">package</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">=</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;ggtree&quot;</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">)</span>\r\n<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">msaplot</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">(</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">ggtree</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">(</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">beast_tree, layout=&quot;unrooted&quot;</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">)</span>, <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">fasta</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">)</span> </code></pre></div><div><br></div><div>Perhaps the best alternative would be to use a geom_point or geom_tippoint and add multiple layers (one for each environment)?</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks for any insights,</div><div><br></div><div>-Matt.</div></div>"
